  "markdown_content": "## Current Situation\\nThe toxic smog season in India's capital has just begun, but those unable to escape cancer-causing poisonous fumes say the hazardous impact on health is already taking its toll.\\n\\nNew Delhi regularly ranks among the world's most polluted capitals, with air quality deteriorating drastically during winter months when cold air traps pollutants from multiple sources including vehicle emissions, industrial activity, construction dust, and agricultural burning.\\n\\n## Health Impacts\\nResidents report increasing respiratory problems, burning eyes, and general malaise as pollution levels spike to dangerous levels. Local hospitals have seen a surge in patients with breathing difficulties, while schools occasionally suspend outdoor activities to protect children.\\n\\n## Government Response\\nDespite government interventions including:\\n* Odd-even vehicle rationing\\n* Construction bans\\n\\nThe city continues to struggle with this annual environmental crisis. Health experts warn of long-term consequences, particularly for vulnerable populations such as children and the elderly.",
